Q(prose("rs_what", f"A swarm of AI agents built a predictor for {len(F)} environmental fate endpoints and a set of toxicity tasks, and then audited it. The predictor accepts three kinds of input: a structure, a structure plus a measured MS/MS spectrum, or a spectrum alone. Each prediction comes with a conformal interval, a domain flag and the EPI Suite value for comparison. Accuracy is the RMSE as a percentage of a naive guess (always predicting the training mean; 100% = no skill). We report it first on leak-free test compounds, i.e. those with no training analogue at Tanimoto >= 0.40."))
Q("\n## Bottom line\n")
Q(prose("rs_bottom", ""))
Q("All of the following comes from one model and one file: the shipped structure+physics model, scored on identical leak-free rows against EPI Suite in `W-MODEL/v5_main/vs_epi.csv`.\n")
Q("| endpoint | n leak-free | ours, % of naive (leak-free) | EPI Suite, same rows | EPI - ours, pp [95% CI] | label noise floor | interval coverage, leak-free (nominal) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for e in sorted(F, key=lambda e: (lf_vals.get(e) is None, lf_vals.get(e) or 0)):
    r = F[e][SHIP]; ee = E.get(e, {})
    _e5 = (E5.get(e) or {}).get("leak_free")
    Q(f"| {e} | {int(_e5['n']) if _e5 else r['leak_free']['n']} | {pc(_e5['model_pct']) if _e5 else pc(r['leak_free']['pct_naive'])} | "
      f"{pc(_e5['epi_pct']) if _e5 else ('no EPI module' if e.startswith('pka') else '-')} | "
      f"{(f'{-_e5[chr(39)+chr(39)] if False else 0:.0f}') if False else (f'{-( _e5[chr(104)+chr(105)] + _e5[chr(108)+chr(111)] )/2:+.1f} [{-_e5[chr(104)+chr(105)]:+.1f}, {-_e5[chr(108)+chr(111)]:+.1f}]' if _e5 else '-')} | "
      f"{pc(NF[e]['pct_naive']) if e in NF else '-'} | {f(_e5['cov'] if _e5 and _e5.get('cov') else r['leak_free'].get('coverage'),2)} ({f(nominal.get(e),2)}) |")
Q(f"\nSkill (below 95% of naive) on leak-free compounds: {lst(skill)}. No skill: {lst(noskill)}. Too few leak-free compounds to score: {lst(eps_unres)}.\n")
Q("## Spectrum only (Fig. 3)\n")
Q(f"From one ESI+ spectrum and no structure the model keeps skill for {lst(so_skill)} and has none for {lst(so_noskill)}. Fragments beat the precursor mass for {lst(so_full_beats_mass)}; a known structure is better for {lst(so_struct_better)}. The rebuilt spectral representation did not beat the Run-2 one (better for {lst(so_new_beats_old)}, worse for {lst(so_old_beats_new)}): a clean negative result for that hypothesis.\n")
Q("## Physics and spectra as add-ons (Fig. 2)\n")
Q(" ".join(f"{v}: leak-free gain with CI excluding zero on {lst(abl_sig(v, 'leak_free', -1))}." for v in abl_var) + " No feature block flattens the rise in error with unfamiliarity. We report this as a negative result.\n")
Q("## Intervals (Fig. 4)\n")
Q((f"Nominal {NOM:.0%}; empirical coverage {cov_lo:.2f}-{cov_hi:.2f} across endpoint x familiarity cells, with {len(under)} cells significantly under nominal" + (": " + "; ".join(f"{e} {b} {c['coverage']:.2f} (n={c['n']})" for e, b, c in under) if under else "") + ". Coverage holds per familiarity bin but not per chemical class (ionizable classes under-cover).\n") if NOM else "")
Q("## Hazard endpoints, on measured labels\n")
Q(f"Three hazard tasks were rebuilt on measured labels (ChEMBL dose-response for receptor potency, CompTox for rat oral LD50); the Run-2 receptor numbers, which scored against another model's consensus calls, are withdrawn. "
  f"As % of the naive training-mean guess on leak-free compounds: rat oral LD50 {f(N['tox_r3']['rat_oral_ld50']['leak_free']['pct_naive'],0)}% (n={N['tox_r3']['rat_oral_ld50']['leak_free']['n']}), oestrogen-receptor potency {f(N['tox_r3']['er_potency']['leak_free']['pct_naive'],0)}% (n={N['tox_r3']['er_potency']['leak_free']['n']}), androgen-receptor potency {f(N['tox_r3']['ar_potency']['leak_free']['pct_naive'],0)}% (n={N['tox_r3']['ar_potency']['leak_free']['n']}). "
  f"For the rare-positive activity calls we report PR-AUC against each familiarity bin's own base rate, never accuracy: in the least familiar bin the oestrogen-receptor model reaches {f(N['tox_r3']['er_active']['by_bin']['<0.3']['pr_auc'],3)} against a base rate of {f(N['tox_r3']['er_active']['by_bin']['<0.3']['base_rate'],3)} (precision {f(N['tox_r3']['er_active']['by_bin']['<0.3']['precision'],2)}, recall {f(N['tox_r3']['er_active']['by_bin']['<0.3']['recall'],2)}). "
  + (f"A control that knows only the similarity bin already reaches PR-AUC " + ", ".join(f"{r['endpoint']} {r['pr_auc_nnsim_only']:.3f}" for r in AD.get('tox_chembl_control', [])) + ", so much of the pooled ranking skill is prevalence drift rather than chemistry.\n" if AD.get('tox_chembl_control') else "\n"))


Q("## What the tool faces outside the test split\n")
_IC, _IP, _ICS = AD.get("inv_cov", []), AD.get("inv_pred", {}), AD.get("inv_cov_sum", {})
if _IC and _IP.get("bin_fraction"):
    Q(f"We scored the two product questions over the EPA inventory rather than the test split: a {_ICS.get('n_sample'):,}-structure random sample for definedness and familiarity, and {_IP['n_predicted']:,} structures through the shipped model. "
      f"{_IP['bin_fraction'].get('<0.3', 0):.0%} of the predicted inventory is below Tanimoto 0.3 to anything we trained on and {_IP['bin_fraction'].get('>=0.7', 0):.0%} is above 0.7 - the reverse of a random test split. "
      f"Up to {max((r.get('A_undefined') or 0) for r in _IC):.1%} of the inventory is physically undefined for the gas-phase endpoints, about four times its share of the labelled data, and a further 7-16% is measurable but not equivalent to our labels; neither is a data gap. "
      "Re-weighting the hazard models by the inventory shows the test split was flattering androgen-receptor potency, and that the oestrogen-receptor intervals under-cover for the typical inventory chemical. "
      "One open problem, stated plainly: at equal Tanimoto similarity the inventory gets far wider intervals than the test set, so a similarity bin does not fully describe how far the inventory has moved from our training data.\n")

Q("## What failed, measured cleanly\n")
_neg = []
_neg.append(f"**Physics is a small, unstable effect.** The set of endpoints where AIMNet2 descriptors beat structure alone with a CI excluding zero changed with every defensible scoring choice (v4: henry, vapour pressure; v5 pre-de-duplication: {lst(AD['physics_sig_sets']['v5_nodedup'])}; v5 de-duplicated: {lst(AD['physics_sig_sets']['v5_dedup'])}), and no feature block flattens the rise of error with unfamiliarity.")
_neg.append("**Rebuilding the spectral representation did not rescue spectra.** Under the same model and the same compounds the rebuilt representation is no better than the Run-2 one; the old representation was not the problem. Spectra also add nothing measurable on top of a known structure.")
_neg.append(f"**The spectral domain flag does not predict error.** Median absolute rank correlation between error and the best-matching training spectrum's cosine similarity is {AD['spec_domain_median_abs_rho']:.3f} across {len(AD['spec_domain'])} endpoints.")
_neg.append("**The model does not know transformation chemistry.** It predicts parent-to-product changes no better than changes between arbitrary similar compounds matched on size and similarity.")
_neg.append(f"**Spectrum-only fails for acute lethality.** The full spectrum reaches {f(AD['ld50_spectrum_only']['arms']['full_spectrum']['pct_of_naive'],1)}% of naive against {f(AD['ld50_spectrum_only']['arms']['structure']['pct_of_naive'],1)}% from the structure on the same {AD['ld50_spectrum_only']['n_test']} compounds - a wide interval around the training mean.")
if AD.get('p004', {}).get('targets'):
    _neg.append("**Our label-fidelity bet (P-004) is falsified.** Models trained on measured receptor potency transferred worse to an external literature benchmark than models trained on another model's consensus labels (paired CIs " + "; ".join(f"{t.replace('_','-')} [{v['delta_ci'][0]:+.3f}, {v['delta_ci'][1]:+.3f}]" for t, v in AD['p004']['targets'].items()) + "); label-space coverage beat label fidelity.")
_neg.append(f"**Our own definedness bookkeeping was wrong for one compound class, and an expert cross-check caught it.** A standardisation step neutralised sulfonate and sulfate salts before the rule that decides whether a property exists was applied, so {Q3['n_changed']} gas-phase and neutral-species cells covering {Q3['n_skeletons_new_class']} skeletons were called defined when they are physically undefined; {Q3['n_labelled_in_changed_cells']} labelled rows are affected. The table was rebuilt, the shipped predictor now refuses those cells, and a related SMARTS defect that gave sodium dodecyl sulfate a basic pKa of 6.6 was found and fixed in the dashboard (`CRITIC/undefined_vs_gap_cells_q003.csv`, `W-TOOL/tool/wtool_postproc.py`).")
_neg.append("**Acidic pKa has no skill on novel chemistry** and EPI Suite's mechanistic AOPWIN beats us on the gas-phase OH rate constant. Both are reported rather than hidden.")
_neg.append("**Tooling that failed:** a vendor AIMNet2 wrapper silently dropped the Coulomb term without Ewald (found and documented by OPS-2); the mechanism-matched open-shell jobs could not run because of a GPU driver/warp incompatibility; an enviPath-based transformation arm could not be built without network access; and logKoa has three leak-free test compounds, too few to score at all.")
for _n in _neg: Q("- " + _n)
Q("")

Q("\n## Data priorities\n")
_vb = AD.get("vod_B_significant", [])
Q("These come from a leave-class-out experiment with a size-matched control, not from counting empty cells: a cell can be empty because the property is physically undefined for that class, and those cells are excluded. "
  + ("The largest measured novelty penalties, in points of naive error, are " + "; ".join(f"{r['cls']} for {r['endpoint']} (+{r['penalty_pp']:.0f} pp, CI {r['penalty_ci']}, n={r['n_test']:.0f})" for r in _vb[:6]) + ". " if _vb else "")
  + "A learning-curve estimate on the same data shows that extra random measurements help familiar chemistry most, so untargeted data collection will not close these gaps; measurements inside the named classes will.\n")

Q("\n## Decisions for the team\n")
Q("1. **Ship the fate endpoints, gate the hazard ones.** The five large fate endpoints beat EPI Suite on compounds with no training analogue and under a graph-partitioned protocol. Receptor activity should be presented as a ranked screen against a stated base rate, never as a call. "
  "2. **Keep the undefined/missing distinction in the product.** Refusing to predict a gas-phase property for a permanently charged species is a feature; counting those cells as data gaps would misdirect measurement money. "
  "3. **Treat spectrum-only as a per-endpoint capability.** It works for logKow, water solubility, vapour pressure and melting point; it does not work for acute lethality, and the intervals under-cover on novel chemistry and need recalibration before release. "
  "4. **Do not invest further in single-conformer physics descriptors** without the conformer-ensemble version; the seed conformer is close to a random draw for flexible molecules. "
  "5. **Fund measurements by class, not by count** - the classes listed above, and a replicate study for BCF, whose label noise floor is the highest we measured.\n")


(H / "review_summary.md").write_text("\n".join(R))

# ================= PDF =================
import markdown
from xhtml2pdf import pisa
CSS = """@page { size: letter; margin: 17mm 15mm 17mm 15mm; @frame footer { -pdf-frame-content: footer; bottom: 6mm; margin-left: 15mm; height: 8mm; } }
body { font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 9.2pt; line-height: 1.35; color: #1f2a33; }
h1 { font-size: 15pt; line-height: 1.2; } h2 { font-size: 12pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccd3d9; margin-top: 10pt; }
h3 { font-size: 10.3pt; margin-top: 8pt; } p { margin: 0 0 5pt 0; }
table { border: 0.5px solid #b0b8bf; font-size: 6.4pt; margin: 3pt 0 6pt 0; } th { background-color: #eef2f5; }
td, th { padding: 1.5pt; border: 0.5px solid #d5dbe0; } code { font-family: Courier; font-size: 7pt; } img { width: 175mm; }"""
def to_pdf(name, title):
    body = markdown.markdown((H / f"{name}.md").read_text(), extensions=["tables", "sane_lists"])
    body = re.sub(r'src="(figures/[^"]+)"', lambda m: f'src="{H / m.group(1)}"', body)
    html = (f"<html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>{title}</title><style>{CSS}</style></head><body>{body}"
            f"<div id='footer' style='font-size:7pt;color:#777'>Plata lab hackathon work on environmental fate and toxicity - draft {datetime.datetime.now():%Y-%m-%d %H:%M} - page <pdf:pagenumber></div></body></html>")
    (H / f"{name}.html").write_text(html)
    with open(H / f"{name}.pdf", "wb") as fh: st = pisa.CreatePDF(html, dest=fh)
    print(name, "pdf errors:", st.err, (H / f"{name}.pdf").stat().st_size)
to_pdf("whitepaper", "Fate and toxicity prediction from structure and/or MS/MS")
to_pdf("review_summary", "Review summary")
print("main figures:", FIGNUM, "supp:", SUPP)
